{"kind":"assert","text":"I read the optional-field ruling and will name the new operation clear(slot, fields). C4 now has six calls. The address keeps only supplied item refs, requires each required ref, and distinguishes omission from an explicit default-valued ref. Edit patches preserve omitted and undefined fields; clear removes only named fields outside the address under the same editing/taken rule. It updates only affected capture, including a default selected at that write, and keeps an empty draft's key. The how-to will explain these rules and JSON-copy behavior. The external decoder successor will admit omitted optional item fields while requiring authored present item fields to match address refs; it will also close the two returned-primary inconsistencies. No checkout or operation implementation has changed. The LS5 gate remains fixed and running.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}